/ A run saved inside Sub, kept in a .plang file (signed by this app) and read back, goes on from its save in an app of its
/ own: Sub's next step reads the context's %name% and its frame's %city%, Record goes on after the call, and the step
/ before the save doesn't run again (%count% comes back 1). The resumed run goes on through this goal too, from the step
/ after `call Record`: the marker, written after the save and never in the snapshot, sends it to Resumed, which writes
/ what it saw and ends it. The asker's own variables are untouched by the resumed run.
Start
- call Record
- if file 'workspace/resumed.marker' exists
    - call Resumed
    - end goal
- write "here" to file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- read file 'workspace/run.plang', write to %snapshot%
- set %seen% = "not yet"
- set %count% = 99
- resume %snapshot%
- assert %seen% equals "not yet"
- assert %count% equals 99
- read file 'workspace/seen.txt', write to %resumed%
- assert %resumed% equals "Alice in Reykjavik 1 yes"
- delete file 'workspace/run.plang'
- delete file 'workspace/resumed.marker'
- delete file 'workspace/seen.txt'

/ The resumed run's end: what it saw, written where the asker reads it.
Resumed
- write "%seen% %count% %unwound%" to file 'workspace/seen.txt'
